      "description": "A circa 1950-1960 image of Independence Square (1950s-1960s) - on the harbour in downtown Tripoli, during the Libyan monarchy era.\nThe present day Martyrs' Square or \"Maidan Al Shohdaa\" , in independent Libya.\nAerial view is to the southwest, with Tripoli Bay in the foreground of the corniche and the two monument columns (before 1960s landfills extended land far into the harbour-bay).\nThe Ottoman era Red Castle (Tripoli Castle museum) is on the upper right, and former Teatro Miramareon the square's lower left.\nAlso formerly named Italian colonial Piazza Italia (1930s-1950s), and Green Square or \"E'saha ElKhadra\" (1970s-mid 2011).",
